{"name":"Contemplative","hex":"#70766a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"contemplative","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Inclined to contemplate; introspective and thoughtful; meditative.","Pertaining to a religious contemplative, or a contemplative religious orders, especially the Roman Catholic varieties."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who has dedicated themselves to religious or philosophical contemplation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/contemplative"}],"entries":[{"title":"Contemplation","blocks":[{"text":"In a religious context, the practice of contemplation seeks a direct awareness of the divine which transcends the intellect, often in accordance with religious practices such as meditation or prayer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/Kampen_kapell_interi%C3%B6r.JPG/330px-Kampen_kapell_interi%C3%B6r.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contemplation"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Solitude.jpg/500px-Solitude.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Solitude.jpg/500px-Solitude.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nature contemplation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASolitude.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Antoine-%C3%89mile_Plassan_-_Devotion_%28Contemplation%29_-_Walters_3745.jpg/500px-Antoine-%C3%89mile_Plassan_-_Devotion_%28Contemplation%29_-_Walters_3745.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Antoine-%C3%89mile_Plassan_-_Devotion_%28Contemplation%29_-_Walters_3745.jpg/1280px-Antoine-%C3%89mile_Plassan_-_Devotion_%28Contemplation%29_-_Walter